<article class="env-definition" id="03TY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03TY">Definition <span data-tag="03TY">64.14.2</span>.</a> With $\Lambda , X, k, K$ as in Definition <a href="/tag/03TX" data-tag="03TX">64.14.1</a>. Since $K\in D_{ctf}(X, \Lambda )$, for any geometric point $\bar x$ of $X$, the complex $K_{\bar x}$ is a perfect complex (in $D_{perf}(\Lambda )$). As we have seen in Section <a href="/tag/03SL" data-tag="03SL">64.3</a>, the Frobenius $\pi _ X$ acts on $K_{\bar x}$. The <em>local Lefschetz number</em> of $K$ is the sum </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \sum \nolimits _{x\in X(k)} \text{Tr}(\pi _ x |_{K_{\overline{x}}})  \]
</div>
  <p> which is again an element of $\Lambda ^\natural $. </p>
</article>